From: renner.dev
Subject: wsi/win32: show only the newest queued image without vsync

The DXGI_SHARED present thread presented every queued image in order. With immediate or mailbox present
modes the application renders faster than the guest compositor takes frames (369 fps against about 250
flips per second, latency scene, Windows 11 guest), so the queue stayed full and a frame reached the
screen as many frames late as the swapchain had images: a key press showed on the fourth flip after it,
16-17 ms median at 240 Hz.

The thread now takes the newest queued image and returns the older ones to the application unshown, as a
mailbox would; FIFO keeps every frame in order.

--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_win32.cpp
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_win32.cpp
@@ -1320,8 +1320,26 @@
       if (chain->present_head == chain->present_tail)
          break; /* quit, and nothing left to present */
 
-      const uint32_t index =
+      uint32_t index =
          chain->present_queue[chain->present_head++ % queue_size];
+      /* Without vsync, only the newest queued image can still be seen: an
+       * older one would be replaced before the next composition. Presenting
+       * each in turn kept the application as many frames behind the display
+       * as it had images (a key showed on the fourth flip after it), so the
+       * older ones go back to the application unshown. Their WSI fences are
+       * waited for when they are presented again (wsi_common_queue_present).
+       */
+      if (chain->base.present_mode == VK_PRESENT_MODE_IMMEDIATE_KHR ||
+          chain->base.present_mode == VK_PRESENT_MODE_MAILBOX_KHR) {
+         bool dropped = false;
+         while (chain->present_head != chain->present_tail) {
+            chain->images[index].state = WSI_IMAGE_IDLE;
+            dropped = true;
+            index = chain->present_queue[chain->present_head++ % queue_size];
+         }
+         if (dropped)
+            u_cnd_monotonic_broadcast(&chain->acquire_cond);
+      }
       mtx_unlock(&chain->acquire_mutex);
       /* Marks the image idle (and records a failure in chain->status). */
       wsi_win32_present_dxgi_shared_now(chain, &chain->images[index], index,
